\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Equilibrium matching does not identify correlations.} For each $\gamma>0$, take the scalar Ornstein--Uhlenbeck thermostat $dX_t=-\gamma X_tdt+\sqrt{2\gamma}\,dW_t$. Its explicit solution is $X_t=e^{-\gamma t}X_0+\sqrt{2\gamma}\int_0^te^{-\gamma(t-s)}dW_s$. If $X_0$ is an independent centered Gaussian of variance one, the variance remains $e^{-2\gamma t}+2\gamma\int_0^te^{-2\gamma(t-s)}ds=1$. Hence every $\gamma$ has the same stationary Gaussian law, but
\[
 \mathbb E[X_tX_0]=e^{-\gamma t},\qquad
 \left.\frac d{dt}\mathbb E[X_tX_0]\right|_{t=0}=-\gamma.
\]
Even the initial correlation slope can be arbitrary while all equilibrium moments agree.

\paragraph{Eliminating a reservoir produces memory.} In the deterministic linear pair $\dot x=-ax+by$, $\dot y=-cy+dx$, $c>0$, solve $y(t)=e^{-ct}y(0)+d\int_0^te^{-c(t-s)}x(s)ds$. Substitution yields an exact convolution term $bd\int_0^te^{-c(t-s)}x(s)ds$ in the resolved equation. Replacing it by an instantaneous feedback requires a time-scale approximation, not merely fitting a stationary variance.

\paragraph{Source-level gap.} These calculations supply explicit counterchecks for equilibrium-only validation and memoryless reservoir closure. They do not specify energetics of the actual unresolved PDE scales, which also needs fluctuation/dissipation and conservation information. The first missing step is a controlled reduction preserving the relevant short-time response and correlations, with a justified vector field and reservoir energy accounting. All dynamical and modeling parts of the source request remain open here.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked stochastic variance and covariance, initial slope and exact reservoir convolution; did not equate invariant-measure accuracy with dynamical accuracy. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked stochastic variance and covariance, initial slope and exact reservoir convolution; did not equate invariant-measure accuracy with dynamical accuracy. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; A controlled subgrid reduction preserving short-time dynamics, correlations and energy accounting is missing.

Coordinator checked stationary Ornstein-Uhlenbeck variance, parameter-dependent correlation and exact eliminated-reservoir memory term. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

